summary:
- topic: Community School Strategy Expansion
  text: The board approved the expansion of the Community School Strategy across the
    district, starting with South Portland High School, aiming to leverage state funding
    and community partnerships to address student needs and improve academic outcomes.
    This strategy, already successful at South Portland Middle School, focuses on
    reducing barriers to education by integrating academics with health, social, and
    community services.
- topic: FY26 Budget and Audit Findings
  text: An update on the FY26 budget revealed that all scenarios project a deficit,
    largely due to a significant shortfall in the nutrition fund. The FY25 audit identified
    material findings related to reconciliation procedures and budgetary non-compliance,
    highlighting the need for improved financial stability and internal controls,
    with confidence expressed that these issues can be addressed over time with stability
    in leadership.
- topic: Superintendent Search Process
  text: The board approved a one-time exception to allow student representatives to
    participate in executive sessions for superintendent semi-finalist interviews,
    under strict confidentiality conditions. This decision aims to incorporate student
    perspectives into the critical selection process for the next superintendent.
- topic: Support for Immigrant Community
  text: "The South Portland School Board formally endorsed the South Portland City\
    \ Council's Resolve # 5\u201325/26, expressing support for the immigrant community\
    \ in response to recent federal immigration enforcement activities. Board members\
    \ emphasized the significant impact on immigrant and asylum students and families,\
    \ and the importance of community and staff support."
- topic: Elementary School Configuration Proposal
  text: A formal proposal for elementary school configuration changes was requested
    for discussion at an upcoming budget workshop. Board members emphasized the need
    for extensive community input and detailed data on potential cost savings and
    impacts, acknowledging the historical significance of neighborhood schools and
    the current budget challenges.
- topic: Pre-Kindergarten and Child Development Services (CDS) Transition
  text: Updates were provided on the pre-K lottery for the upcoming school year and
    the district's transition to join Cohort 3 of the Child Development Services (CDS)
    for 4-year-olds, which will bring additional state funding. Discussions also covered
    existing and potential partnerships with childcare providers and Headstart to
    expand pre-K access.
- topic: Athletic Complex Update
  text: An update on the athletic complex project detailed the scope, including a
    new eight-lane track, natural grass field, new lights, and permanent restrooms.
    The timeline projects completion by September 2027, with potential delays contingent
    on state permitting processes related to impervious surface area.
